Dragontamer wrote:
>
> So tins of meat can rot? I thought they were fresh forever...

Rotten and spoiled are completely different things.

Spoiled meat gives the ULCH message.  You get food poisoning
and you die from it unless cured.  Canning takes spoiled or
unspoiled meat to unspoiled.  Canned meat never spoils.

Rotten meat gives less nutrition.  Sometimes it confuses you
or causes you to pass out.  If there are no monsters in range
it is safe to eat rotten food - Just another bit of Nethack
strategy that eating is a risky activity and it needs to be done
in safety.

Any food has a chance of being rotten when you try to eat
it.  Cursed food is always rotten.  Uncursed has a medium
chance of being rotten.  Blessed food has a low but not zero
chance if I read the code right.  Each time you eat an item
out of a stack the chances get rolled again, so don't toss a
stack if one is rotten.  One rotten apple does not spoil the
barrel.  I think eggs do all rot in stacks though.

Also corpses rot away and no longer exist.  This is yet
another useage of the word "rot" and it is not to be confused
with the randomly determined rotten status.  A blessed
corpse takes longer to disappear, but it still goes spoiled and
I think will still cause fatal food poisoning.



